{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Customer Relationship Management"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about customer relationship management."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Build the IT system prototype, starting from the analysis of the functional characteristics of the system regarding user-friendliness, functionality and user experience, supported in software applied following design protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about analytical CRM."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe what analytical CRM is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster showing the importance of analytical CRM."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your research to your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research information about analytical CRM."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can describe what analytical CR is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster about analytical CRM."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my ideas to my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "purpose "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "objective, goal or aim"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The purpose is to know well your customers to provide the products, services and contact they need."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "devote "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to dedicate or consecrate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Another important aspect is that we can use some software that is devoted entirely to this"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unreliable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that can't be trusted, unstable or undependable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was a little unreliable as well, because it didn't keep track of all transactions, and we also experienced data loss sometimes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "data loss "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the impossibility to retrieve or find data "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was a little unreliable as well, because it didn't keep track of all transactions, and we also experienced data loss sometimes. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cloud-based "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that can be stored on online services or the internet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The CRM system they got was also cloud-based, and made everything much easier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "loyal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "faithful towards someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We want them to feel like we know them well, like a small shop owner would know his most loyal customers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past (Review)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the<span class= \"strong\"> simple past</span>  tense to talk about actions or events that started and finished in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was a little unreliable as well, because it didn't keep track of all transactions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, once they updated it, they divided the work on areas like sales, marketing and services."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to use this tense, you need a subject and the past form of the verb. Don't forget that we have two different types of verbs, regular and irregular ones, and that each one of them has a different type conjugation.<br>Regular verbs only add a final \u201c-ed\u201d in order to conjugate them in the past form.  <br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br><span class= \"italic\">  The CRM platform <span class= \"strong\"> completed</span>  the operation successfully. We <span class= \"strong\"> started</span>  to learn about CRM. </span> <br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, irregular verbs do not follow any specific rule as they can change independently. <br> <br>  Examples:<br><span class= \"italic\">  The company <span class= \"strong\"> bought</span>  a great CRM management tool.<br> They <span class= \"strong\"> felt</span>  ready to implement a new CRM management tool. </span>  <br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, keep in mind that for those types of verbs, the structure that we follow to write negative statements is always the same. We have to use the auxiliary verb \u201cdid\u201d; plus, when we use it, we do not conjugate the action verb. <br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br><span class= \"italic\">  The CRM platform <span class= \"strong\"> didn't complete</span>  the operation successfully. <br> The company <span class= \"strong\"> didn't buy</span>  a great CRM management tool.</span>  <br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Finally, you just have to move the position of the auxiliary verb to transform the sentence into an interrogative one. Furthermore, we can add a WH- word at the beginning to create open questions (whose answer is not yes/no). <br><br>  Example: <br><span class= \"italic\">  <span class= \"strong\"> Did</span>  the CRM platform <span class= \"strong\"> complete</span>  the operation successfully? <br> <span class= \"strong\"> What did</span>  the company <span class= \"strong\"> decide</span>  to buy?</span> <br>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to in Affirmative and Negative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the expression <span class= \"strong\">used to</span>  to talk about past habits, actions that we regularly did in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, they used to have a very complicated system before. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, they didn't use to store anything online until they updated the system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is important to take into account that when we use the expression used to we are mentioning a recurrent action that took place in the past, but that does not take place in the present time. The structure that we follow to write affirmative sentences using this expression is: <br><br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class= \"strong\"> used to + verb in infinitive</span>  + complement. </div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <span class= \"italic\"> <br> We <span class= \"strong\"> used to use</span>  a very basic CRM management tool. <br> They <span class= \"strong\"> used to believe</span>  that CRM was not an important part of a business. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to write a negative statement using this expression, you have to be careful as the structure changes: <br><br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class= \"strong\"> did not (didn't) + use to* + verb in infinitive</span>  + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "*Pay attention to the conjugation of <span class= \"strong\"> used to</span> . As we have the auxiliary verb <span class= \"strong\"> did</span>  in its negative form, we do not conjugate the verb. That is why we write <span class= \"strong\"> use to</span> . "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<span class= \"italic\"> <br> We <span class= \"strong\"> didn't use to use</span>  a very basic CRM management tool. <br> They <span class= \"strong\"> didn't use to believe</span>  that CRM was an important part of a business. </span> "}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss the concept of customer relationship management."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give precise information about customer relationship management."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what to do to know your customers in a business."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Is it important to divide responsibilities in the logistics industry? How?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can you optimize processes in the imports process of a company? Explain. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attemp